## DESCRIPTION
## Generates a random 3x3 zero-one matrix representing a relation and asks to compute the
## matrix representation of the inverse and complement of the relation.
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject(Discrete Math)
## DBchapter(Discete Structures)
## DBsection(Matrices)
## Date(06/03/2026)
## Institution(Louisiana Tech University)
## Author(Jason Terry)
## KEYWORDS('discrete math','matrix','boolean','inverse','complement','relation')

DOCUMENT();

## Load libraries
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

## Set the context for matrices
Context("Matrix");

## Create a random 3x3 boolean matrix
$A = Matrix([
    [ random(0, 1, 1), random(0, 1, 1), random(0, 1, 1) ],
    [ random(0, 1, 1), random(0, 1, 1), random(0, 1, 1) ],
    [ random(0, 1, 1), random(0, 1, 1), random(0, 1, 1) ]
]);

## Create the matrices representing the inverse and complement relation
$inverse = $A->transpose;

$ones = Matrix([ [ 1, 1, 1 ], [ 1, 1, 1 ], [ 1, 1, 1 ] ]);

$comp = $ones - $A;

BEGIN_PGML

Suppose the matrix representation for relation [` R `] is [` M_{R} = [$A] `]. Compute the matrix represenation for the inverse relation [` M_{R^{-1}} `] and the complement relation [` M_{\overline{R}} `].

[`` M_{R^{-1}} ``] = [___]*{$inverse}

[`` M_{\overline{R}} ``] = [___]*{$comp}

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
Solutions: 

[`` M_{R^{-1}} = [$inverse] ``]

[`` M_{\overline{R}}  = [$comp]  ``]

END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
